  "prompt": "How's the surf in Siargao this week?",
  "keywords": [],
  "text": "## Siargao surf this week (sample data)\n\nSmall and friendly early in the week, a bigger swell from Thursday. Light offshore winds before 9am.\n\n**Best for beginners**\n- **Jacking Horse** (Beginner, sand and reef): 1 to 2 ft all week. Soft rolling waves next to Cloud 9, best at mid to high tide.\n- **Quiksilver** (Beginner to intermediate): 2 to 3 ft, cleanest before 9am. Easy paddle out from the Cloud 9 area.\n\n**For experienced surfers**\n- **Cloud 9** (Advanced, shallow reef): 3 to 5 ft from Thursday. Fast right-hand barrels, crowded at dawn.\n- **Stimpy's** (Advanced, boat access): 4 to 6 ft lefts on the outer reef. Go with a local boatman and a buddy.\n\n**Surf costs (sample prices)**\n- Surf lesson, 1.5 hours with coach: PHP 1,500\n- Softboard rental, full day: PHP 500\n- Boat to the outer reefs, per person: PHP 1,000\n\n**Safety:** Cloud 9 and Stimpy's break over shallow reef. Wear reef booties, never surf them at low tide, and stay out of the lineup at Cloud 9 if you are still learning.",
